# Fixture for the quick-fix path with an INFERRED-TYPE local, which is the
# dominant style in this codebase. Vector is a real class in gen_collect.obl but
# is not in scope without a 'use', so analysis reports "Undefined class ..." --
# the one diagnostic Document.CodeAction offers a fix for.
#
# This form produced no fixes at all until #1057. Two reasons: the class name
# was read from between the first and last quote of the message, and this form's
# message carries a bundle hint containing more quotes; and an inferred local has
# no symbol-table entry to match, because the entry is created during type
# inference and analysis aborts on this very undefined class. The fix keys off
# the diagnostic being anchored on the class token, which the sibling
# lsp_codeaction_declared.obs is not -- see the note there.
class NeedsUse {
	function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
		v := Vector->New()<IntRef>;
		v->Size()->PrintLine();
	}
}
